# Electronic energy levels for 11-species air
#
# For use with:  species air.species <sp1 sp2 ...> elecfile air.elec
#                collide_modify electronic discrete
#                fix <ID> elecmode
#
# format: species-ID N  temp1 relax1 degen1 spin1 dof1  ...  tempN relaxN degenN spinN dofN
#   temp  = state energy above the species ground state / kB (K)
#   relax = inverse electronic relaxation collision number (per-collision
#           relaxation probability under "collide_modify relax constant");
#           the 0.01 used here is a nominal default - calibrate to a
#           state-resolved kinetics dataset for quantitative excitation work
#   degen = total degeneracy of the level (sum of 2J+1 over grouped states)
#   spin  = spin-multiplicity class (2S+1) used by per-partner spin
#           conservation; for a grouped level it is the multiplicity of the
#           group's lowest state, so spin conservation across grouped levels
#           is approximate
#   dof   = unused (0)
#
# Level data: atoms (N, O, N+, O+) from the NIST Atomic Spectra Database;
# molecules from Huber & Herzberg, "Constants of Diatomic Molecules" (1979),
# as reproduced by the NIST Chemistry WebBook (term energies T_e).
# E[K] = E[cm^-1] * 1.4387769.  Checked against both sources 2026-11.
#
# Dense manifolds are GROUPED:
#   degeneracy = sum of 2J+1 (atoms) or of the state degeneracies
#                (molecules) over the group's states
#   energy     = the LOWEST state energy of the group (excitation is most
#                sensitive to the threshold, so grouping is conservative)
# The ground-term fine structure of O, N+, NO and O2+ is lumped at 0 K.
# This overstates the electronic partition function at low temperature:
# by 9-14% at 1000 K, 1.7-2.8% at 5000 K and 0.9-1.4% at 10000 K (O 11%,
# 2.2%, 1.1%).
#
# Molecules: every state with a definite T_e below the dissociation limit,
# and the bound states slightly above it that correlate to excited-atom
# products (N2 C3Pi_u, O2 B3Sigma_u-, NO D2Sigma+).  States whose T_e
# Huber & Herzberg give only as uncertain (in parentheses) are left out -
# N2 A'5Sigma_g+, G3Delta_g, C''5Pi_u, E3Sigma_g+; N2+ a4Sigma_u+; O2+
# b'4Pi_g, C2Phi_u - except the NO quartets a4Pi and b4Sigma- and O2
# A'3Delta_u (in the Herzberg group).  Including them would raise the
# electronic partition function at 20000 K by 14% (N2+), 7% (O2+) and
# 3% (N2).
#
# Atoms: the levels of the ground and low configurations, and the excited
# configurations up to 4s and 3d on the lowest parent term (N, O) or up to
# 2p3s and the 2s2p^n terms (N+, O+); the higher Rydberg levels are left
# out.  The N and O partition functions then agree with those of the CEA
# database (Gurvich level sets) within 0.5% up to 20000 K, apart from the
# O fine structure; all levels the ASD lists below the ionization limit
# would raise them by about 5% at 20000 K and 40% at 30000 K.
#
# The electron (e) carries no internal electronic ladder and is deliberately
# absent: its spin degeneracy (g = 2) enters the Saha equation for
# ionization equilibria, not the internal-energy relaxation model.
#
# Molecules ---------------------------------------------------------------
# N2:  X1Sg+ | A3Su+ | B3Pg+W3Du | B'3Su-+a'1Su-+a1Pg+w1Du | C3Pu
# O2:  X3Sg- | a1Dg | b1Sg+ | Herzberg c1Su-+A'3Du+A3Su+ | B3Su-
# NO:  X2Pi (both spin-orbit components, g=4) | a4Pi | A2S++B2Pi | b4S- | C2Pi+D2S+
# N2+: X2Sg+ | A2Pu | B2Su+ | D2Pg | C2Su+
# O2+: X2Pg (both spin-orbit components, g=4) | a4Pu | A2Pu | b4Sg-
# NO+: X1S+ | a3S+ | b3Pi+w3D | b'3S-+A'1S+ | W1D | A1Pi

N2  5   0.0 0.01 1 1 0   72232.0 0.01 3 3 0   85778.0 0.01 12 3 0   95350.0 0.01 8 3 0   128248.0 0.01 6 3 0
O2  5   0.0 0.01 3 3 0   11392.0 0.01 2 1 0   18985.0 0.01 1 1 0   47562.0 0.01 10 1 0   71642.0 0.01 3 3 0
NO  5   0.0 0.01 4 2 0   55307.0 0.01 8 4 0   63257.0 0.01 6 2 0   70040.0 0.01 4 4 0   74998.0 0.01 6 2 0
N2+ 5   0.0 0.01 2 2 0   13190.0 0.01 4 2 0   36633.0 0.01 2 2 0   75274.0 0.01 4 2 0   92958.0 0.01 2 2 0
O2+ 4   0.0 0.01 4 2 0   47428.0 0.01 8 4 0   58514.0 0.01 4 2 0   71294.0 0.01 4 4 0
NO+ 6   0.0 0.01 1 1 0   75090.0 0.01 3 3 0   85233.0 0.01 12 3 0   97434.0 0.01 4 3 0   102801.0 0.01 2 1 0   105709.0 0.01 2 1 0

# Atoms -------------------------------------------------------------------
# N:  4So | 2Do | 2Po | 3s4P+3s2P+2s2p4-4P | 3p manifold+(1D)3s2D | (3P)4s+(3P)3d
# O:  3P (fine structure grouped, g=9) | 1D | 1S | 3s5So | 3s3So | 3p5P+3p3P | (4So)4s+(4So)3d
# N+: 3P (fine structure grouped, g=9) | 1D | 1S | 2s2p3-5So | 2s2p3-3Do | 2s2p3-3Po |
#     2s2p3-1Do+3So+1Po + 2p3s-3Po+1Po
# O+: 4So | 2Do | 2Po | 2s2p4-4P | 2s2p4-2D | (3P)3s-4P+2P + 2s2p4-2S+2P

N   6   0.0 0.01 4 4 0   27660.0 0.01 10 2 0   41493.0 0.01 6 2 0   119827.0 0.01 30 4 0   134643.0 0.01 64 2 0   149090.0 0.01 108 4 0
O   7   0.0 0.01 9 3 0   22830.0 0.01 5 1 0   48620.0 0.01 1 1 0   106136.0 0.01 5 5 0   110491.0 0.01 3 3 0   124635.0 0.01 24 5 0   137370.0 0.01 48 5 0
N+  7   0.0 0.01 9 3 0   22037.0 0.01 5 1 0   47032.0 0.01 1 1 0   67313.0 0.01 5 5 0   132708.0 0.01 15 3 0   157138.0 0.01 9 3 0   207454.0 0.01 23 1 0
O+  6   0.0 0.01 4 4 0   38574.0 0.01 10 2 0   58224.0 0.01 6 2 0   172419.0 0.01 12 4 0   238820.0 0.01 10 2 0   266512.0 0.01 26 4 0
